EXAM_DATA.papers["2009"] = {"id":"2009","year":2009,"label":"2009 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2009/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Research on animal intelligence always makes us wonder just how smart humans are.   {{1}}   the fruit-fly experiments described by Carl Zimmer in the Science Times. Fruit flies who were taught to be smarter than the average fruit fly   {{2}}   to live shorter lives. This suggests that   {{3}}   bulbs burn longer, that there is a(n)   {{4}}   in not being too bright."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"Intelligence, it   {{5}}   , is a high-priced option. It takes more upkeep, burns more fuel and is slow   {{6}}   the starting line because it depends on learning – a(n)   {{7}}   process – instead of instinct. Plenty of other species are able to learn, and one of the things they've apparently learned is when to   {{8}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"Is there an adaptive value to   {{9}}   intelligence? That's the question behind this new research. Instead of casting a wistful glance   {{10}}   at all the species we've left in the dust I.Q.-wise, it implicitly asks what the real   {{11}}   of our own intelligence might be. This is   {{12}}   the mind of every animal we've ever met."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"Research on animal intelligence also makes us wonder what experiments animals would   {{13}}   on humans if they had the chance. Every cat with an owner,   {{14}}   , is running a small-scale study in operant conditioning. We believe that   {{15}}   animals ran the labs, they would test us to   {{16}}   the limits of our patience, our faithfulness, our memory for locations. They would try to decide what intelligence in humans is really   {{17}}   , not merely how much of it there is.   {{18}}   , they would hope to study a(n)   {{19}}   question: Are humans actually aware of the world they live in?   {{20}}   the results are inconclusive."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Suppose"},{"key":"B","text":"Consider"},{"key":"C","text":"Observe"},{"key":"D","text":"Imagine"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"宾语是真实的果蝇实验 空后宾语是the fruit-fly experiments described by Carl Zimmer in the Science Times.，这是一个真实发生、已被报道的实验，不是假想或假设。这就排除了表“假想”的 Suppose/Imagine。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Suppose意为“假设”，后接虚拟情境，与“真实存在的实验”冲突。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Consider意为“试想/请看”，常用于将一个真实存在的例证摆到读者面前作为论据，正合此处用果蝇实验切入论题的语境。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Observe强调亲身观察，而读者并未亲历该实验，只是被请去“考虑/正视”一份已被报道的实验。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Imagine意为“想象”，后接虚构画面，与“已被报道的真实实验”不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tended"},{"key":"B","text":"feared"},{"key":"C","text":"happened"},{"key":"D","text":"threatened"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"实验现象的普遍结论 本句Fruit flies who were taught to be smarter than the average fruit fly __(2)__ to live shorter lives.是在陈述实验里聪明果蝇普遍出现的结果，下一句紧接This suggests that __(3)__ bulbs burn longer进一步抽象，可见这是一个倾向性结论。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"tended to do 表“总体倾向于”，与“聪明的果蝇普遍寿命更短”这一实验结论吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"feared意为“害怕”，主语果蝇无此主观情绪，且与中性的实验描述基调不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"happened to do 表“碰巧”，强调偶然一次，与实验得出的群体性规律相悖。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"threatened to do 通常意为“扬言要做”，与无意志的果蝇及客观陈述不搭。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"thinner"},{"key":"B","text":"stabler"},{"key":"C","text":"lighter"},{"key":"D","text":"dimmer"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"聪明对应明亮 上一句说to live shorter lives——聪明的果蝇活得短，本句用__(3)__ bulbs burn longer作类比，并紧接that there is a(n) __(4)__ in not being too bright.，其中 bright 既指“明亮”也指“聪明”，反向暗示本空应是“不那么亮”的灯泡。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"thinner指“更薄”，与“聪明/迟钝”这一对照无关联。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"stabler指“更稳定”，无法与下一句的 bright 形成呼应。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"lighter意为“更亮/更轻”，若取“更亮”反而与“迟钝—长寿”这条主线相反，正话反说。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"dimmer意为“更暗的”，与下一句的 bright 形成对照，对应“不那么聪明”，恰好支撑“迟钝的灯泡烧得更久”这一比喻。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tendency"},{"key":"B","text":"advantage"},{"key":"C","text":"inclination"},{"key":"D","text":"priority"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"迟钝带来好处 上文This suggests that __(3)__ bulbs burn longer已把“迟钝的灯泡”与“烧得久（活得久）”挂钩，本句there is a(n) __(4)__ in not being too bright.需要一个名词承接“不太聪明竟然是一种____”的判断，指向“好处、优势”一类词义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"tendency意为“倾向”，是中性描述，无法表达“反而是件好事”的判断。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"advantage意为“优势/好处”，对应上文“迟钝反而活得久”这一正向结论，且 there is an advantage in doing 是固定表达。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"inclination意为“偏爱/倾向”，描述主观偏好，与客观“好处”不同。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"priority意为“优先事项”，与“好处”不同，无法承接反差结论。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"insists on"},{"key":"B","text":"sums up"},{"key":"C","text":"turns out"},{"key":"D","text":"puts forward"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"5.","reason":"插入语转述结论 本句Intelligence, it __(5)__, is a high-priced option.是对前文实验结论的转述：把上一段果蝇实验得出的“聪明有代价”抽象为一般结论。插入语承担“原来/结果证明”之意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"insists on意为“坚持”，需要明确施动主语，与 it 作形式主语的插入语结构不搭。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"sums up意为“总结”，不能放在“, it ___,”这种插入语位置作“结果证明”用。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"turns out意为“结果证明是”，是“, it turns out,”这种插入语的标准搭配，恰好引出对前段实验的概括结论。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"puts forward意为“提出（观点）”，需具体施动主语，与插入语结构冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"off"},{"key":"B","text":"behind"},{"key":"C","text":"over"},{"key":"D","text":"along"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"起跑线的语境暗示 is slow __(6)__ the starting line because it depends on learning里的 starting line 是赛跑比喻；后文给出原因——智力依赖学习，所以“起步”慢。所需介词须能搭配“起步/离开起跑线”。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"off the starting line 是固定表达，意为“起跑/离开起跑线”，slow off the starting line 即“起步慢”，与下句“依赖学习”因果一致。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"behind the starting line 字面是“在起跑线后”，无标准英语习语表“起步慢”。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"over the starting line 表“越过起跑线”，已是开跑之后，与“起步慢”逻辑相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"along the starting line 表“沿起跑线”，方向上不指起步动作，搭配不成立。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"incredible"},{"key":"B","text":"spontaneous"},{"key":"C","text":"inevitable"},{"key":"D","text":"gradual"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"7.","reason":"学习与本能对照 because it depends on learning – a(n) __(7)__ process – instead of instinct.中 instead of instinct 是关键：本能是瞬发的，与之相对的 learning 必须是“渐进/逐步”的，方能解释为何“起步慢”。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"incredible意为“难以置信的”，描述主观感受，与本能/学习的对照无关。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"spontaneous意为“自发的、本能的”，恰是本能的属性，与 learning 反义不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"inevitable意为“不可避免的”，与“慢”和“依赖学习”的逻辑无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"gradual意为“逐步的、渐进的”，正好刻画学习相较于本能的“一步步累积”特征，解释“起步慢”。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fight"},{"key":"B","text":"doubt"},{"key":"C","text":"stop"},{"key":"D","text":"think"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"动物学会的是停下 Plenty of other species are able to learn, and one of the things they've apparently learned is when to __(8)__.说其他物种也会学习，它们学会的恰恰是“何时 ___”。结合前面there is a(n) __(4)__ in not being too bright，物种学到的是知道何时止步，而不是何时再思考。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"fight意为“争斗”，与“别太聪明”这条主线无关。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"doubt意为“怀疑”，反而是更费脑的活动，与“何必太聪明”相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"stop意为“停下”，when to stop（知道何时止步）正是对前文“别太聪明有好处”的延伸。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"think意为“思考”，与全段“聪明是高代价”的主线相反，是干扰陷阱。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"invisible"},{"key":"B","text":"limited"},{"key":"C","text":"indefinite"},{"key":"D","text":"different"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"止步对应有限 when to __(8)__承上，Is there an adaptive value to __(9)__ intelligence?承下：止步意味着不无限地用智力，对应“有限度的智力”。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"invisible意为“看不见的”，与“何时止步”无关联。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"limited意为“有限的”，承接上句“知道何时止步”，引出本段反思“有限度的智力是否反而有适应价值”。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"indefinite意为“无限期的、不确定的”，与“何时止步”逻辑相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"different意为“不同的”，过于宽泛，没有承接上文“止步”的具体含义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"upward"},{"key":"B","text":"forward"},{"key":"C","text":"afterward"},{"key":"D","text":"backward"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"回望被甩在身后的物种 casting a wistful glance __(10)__ at all the species we've left in the dust I.Q.-wise中 left in the dust 表示“被远远甩在身后”。要怀念地看这些已被甩开的对象，必须向后看。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"upward向上，与“甩在身后”方位不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"forward向前，与“向身后那些物种投以一瞥”矛盾。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"afterward指“随后”，是时间副词，不修饰 glance 的方向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"backward意为“向后”，glance backward at … 正是“回头望向…”，对应被甩在身后的物种。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"features"},{"key":"B","text":"influences"},{"key":"C","text":"results"},{"key":"D","text":"costs"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"11.","reason":"高价选项的人类版 Intelligence, it __(5)__, is a high-priced option.已把 intelligence 定性为高价之物；it implicitly asks what the real __(11)__ of our own intelligence might be.在同一主线上追问人类智力的“真实代价”。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"features意为“特点”，描述中性，未回扣“高价”主线。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"influences意为“影响”，方向不明，未指向代价。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"results意为“结果”，关注后效，不等于“成本”。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"costs意为“代价”，紧扣 high-priced option，将动物层面的代价类比到人类，主线一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"outside"},{"key":"B","text":"on"},{"key":"C","text":"by"},{"key":"D","text":"across"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"12.","reason":"动物心头惦记着的问题 This is __(12)__ the mind of every animal we've ever met.意在说前文那个反问“人类智力的真正代价是什么”，是每只动物都惦记着的问题。be on one's mind 是固定搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"outside one's mind 不构成固定搭配，逻辑也不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"on one's mind 是固定习语，表“惦记着”，正合此句意。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"by the mind of 不构成习语。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"across one's mind 多用于 cross sb.'s mind（闪过心头）而非 across。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"deliver"},{"key":"B","text":"carry"},{"key":"C","text":"perform"},{"key":"D","text":"apply"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"13.","reason":"对人类做实验 what experiments animals would __(13)__ on humans if they had the chance.要表达“动物会对人类做什么实验”，介词是 on，动词需与 experiments…on 形成固定搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"deliver意为“递送/发表”，不与 experiments 搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"carry 必须搭 out 才能构成 carry out an experiment，单用 carry 不与 experiments 搭。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"perform experiments on sb 是地道搭配，意为“对某人做实验”。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"apply 后通常接“理论/方法”，并搭配 to，不直接接 experiments on。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"by chance"},{"key":"B","text":"in contrast"},{"key":"C","text":"as usual"},{"key":"D","text":"for instance"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"14.","reason":"猫例呼应一般论断 上一句Research on animal intelligence also makes us wonder what experiments animals would __(13)__ on humans if they had the chance.提出一般论断；本句Every cat with an owner, __(14)__, is running a small-scale study in operant conditioning.立刻给出“每只有主人的猫”这一具体例子。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"by chance意为“偶然”，无法承接“给个例子”的逻辑。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in contrast意为“与之相反”，上下句不是对比关系。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"as usual意为“一如既往”，不表举例。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"for instance意为“例如”，恰好把“有主人的猫”作为上一句论断的例子引出。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"if"},{"key":"B","text":"unless"},{"key":"C","text":"as"},{"key":"D","text":"lest"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"15.","reason":"would 触发虚拟条件 __(15)__ animals ran the labs, they would test us：主句 they would test us 是 would do，从句 ran the labs 是一般过去式，构成 if 引导的与现在事实相反的虚拟条件句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"if引导虚拟条件句，与 would test 形成“假如…就会…”的对应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"unless意为“除非”，会把意思变成“除非动物管实验室，否则会测试我们”，逻辑混乱。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"as通常引时间/原因从句，不引虚拟条件。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"lest意为“以免”，与“假如”的逻辑相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"moderate"},{"key":"B","text":"overcome"},{"key":"C","text":"determine"},{"key":"D","text":"reach"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"16.","reason":"测试以确定极限 they would test us to __(16)__ the limits of our patience, our faithfulness, our memory for locations.，test 是手段，目的应是“查明、确定”这些极限到底有多大。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"moderate意为“缓和”，与“测试目的”不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"overcome意为“克服”，动物并非要克服人类的极限。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"determine意为“查明/确定”，正好作为 test 的目的：摸清耐心、忠诚、空间记忆的极限。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"reach 后接极限时多表“达到极限”，主语应是被测者本身，逻辑不顺。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"at"},{"key":"B","text":"for"},{"key":"C","text":"after"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"17.","reason":"真正用来做什么 They would try to decide what intelligence in humans is really __(17)__, not merely how much of it there is.中 not merely how much of it there is 提示对比的不是数量，而是“真正的用途/作用”，即 what X is for。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"at 不构成 what … at 的“用途”习语。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"for 与 what … for 构成习语“…是用来做什么的”，正合本句“真正的智力是用来做什么”。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"after 不与 what 构成用途疑问，搭配不成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"with 不构成 what … with 表“用途”的习语，与本意不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Above all"},{"key":"B","text":"After all"},{"key":"C","text":"However"},{"key":"D","text":"Otherwise"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"18.","reason":"升级到最重要的问题 前句They would try to decide what intelligence in humans is really __(17)__, not merely how much of it there is.已经在追问“真正的用途”；后句they would hope to study a(n) __(19)__ question: Are humans actually aware of the world they live in?进一步把镜头推到“最根本的问题”。这是层层递进，把“最最关键”的问题挑出来。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Above all意为“最重要的是”，正好把后面那个“人类是否真正意识到自己所处世界”的根本问题挑出来。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"After all意为“毕竟”，引出解释或让步原因，与递进到最关键问题不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"However意为“然而”，前后不是对立关系，是递进关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Otherwise意为“否则”，前后无因果假设关系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fundamental"},{"key":"B","text":"comprehensive"},{"key":"C","text":"equivalent"},{"key":"D","text":"hostile"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"根本问题对应根本词 __(18)__, they would hope to study a(n) __(19)__ question: Are humans actually aware of the world they live in?，冒号后揭示的问题是“人类是否真正意识到所处世界”——这是带哲学色彩的根本性问题，空处应填一个表示“根本的”的形容词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"fundamental意为“根本的”，与 Above all 的递进高潮以及后文哲学性反问完全契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"comprehensive意为“全面的”，关注面广，但不强调“最根本”，与 Above all 不对位。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"equivalent意为“等同的”，与 question 搭配无意义。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"hostile意为“敌对的”，色彩词不符合科学反思的中性基调。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"By accident"},{"key":"B","text":"In time"},{"key":"C","text":"So far"},{"key":"D","text":"Better still"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"迄今结论尚无 __(20)__ the results are inconclusive.作结尾句，呼应全文反讽：对“人类是否真意识到所处世界”这一根本问题，至今没有定论。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"By accident意为“偶然”，与“结果尚无定论”的中性时间状语不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"In time意为“及时”，与“至今无定论”不搭。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"So far意为“迄今为止”，自然搭配“研究结果仍无定论”，作为全文收尾。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Better still意为“更妙的是”，引出补充优势，与“无定论”相反。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"Habits are a funny thing. We reach for them mindlessly, setting our brains on auto-pilot and relaxing into the unconscious comfort of familiar routine. \"Not choice, but habit rules the unreflecting herd,\" William Wordsworth said in the 19th century. In the ever-changing 21st century, even the word \"habit\" carries a negative implication."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"So it seems paradoxical to talk about habits in the same context as creativity and innovation. But brain researchers have discovered that when we consciously develop new habits, we create parallel paths, and even entirely new brain cells, that can jump our trains of thought onto new, innovative tracks."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"Rather than dismissing ourselves as unchangeable creatures of habit, we can instead direct our own change by consciously developing new habits. In fact, the more new things we try – the more we step outside our comfort zone – the more inherently creative we become, both in the workplace and in our personal lives."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"But don't bother trying to kill off old habits; once those ruts of procedure are worn into the brain, they're there to stay. Instead, the new habits we deliberately press into ourselves create parallel pathways that can bypass those old roads."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"\"The first thing needed for innovation is a fascination with wonder,\" says Dawna Markova, author of The Open Mind. \"But we are taught instead to 'decide', just as our president calls himself 'the Decider'.\" She adds, however, that \"to decide is to kill off all possibilities but one. A good innovational thinker is always exploring the many other possibilities.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"All of us work through problems in ways of which we're unaware, she says. Researchers in the late 1960s discovered that humans are born with the capacity to approach challenges in four primary ways: analytically, procedurally, relationally (or collaboratively) and innovatively. At the end of adolescence, however, the brain shuts down half of that capacity, preserving only those modes of thought that have seemed most valuable during the first decade or so of life."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-7","text":"The current emphasis on standardized testing highlights analysis and procedure, meaning that few of us inherently use our innovative and collaborative modes of thought. \"This breaks the major rule in the American belief system – that anyone can do anything,\" explains M. J. Ryan, author of the 2006 book This Year I Will… and Ms. Markova's business partner. \"That's a lie that we have perpetuated, and it fosters commonness. Knowing what you're good at and doing even more of it creates excellence.\" This is where developing new habits comes in."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"In Wordsworth's view, \"habits\" is characterized by being____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"casual."},{"key":"B","text":"familiar."},{"key":"C","text":"mechanical."},{"key":"D","text":"changeable."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在Wordsworth看来，\"习惯\"的特点是____","choicesZh":{"A":"随意的","B":"熟悉的","C":"机械的","D":"易变的"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 In Wordsworth's view, \"habits\" is characterized by being 问的是 Wordsworth 的原话怎么形容 habits，是对引文中形容词的直接复述，不需要推断。","parse":"Q21 是不完整陈述句，等待选项作表语。介词短语 In Wordsworth's view 是状语，主语是 \"habits\"，谓语 is characterized by being 是「以……为特征」的被动结构，选项填入 being 之后的形容词。无陷阱。","locateEn":"\"Not choice, but habit rules the unreflecting herd,\" William Wordsworth said in the 19th century.","locateZh":"「统治不加思考的人群的，不是选择，而是习惯，」威廉·华兹华斯于 19 世纪如是说。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"casual 意为「随意、漫不经心的」，而 Wordsworth 强调的是习惯之「规则性、支配性」（rules），二者方向相反；原文也没有任何信息支持「随意」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"familiar 是 P1 段首作者自己的描述 the unconscious comfort of familiar routine，而非 Wordsworth 的观点；本题题干明确限定 In Wordsworth's view，张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判到「无需思考的自动反应」后，对照四项，唯有 mechanical 在语义上能涵盖「unreflecting」的「无意识、自动」之义，故选 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"the unreflecting herd","opt":"mechanical"},{"orig":"Not choice, but habit rules","opt":"mechanical"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"changeable 意为「易变的」，与 Wordsworth 言下之意「习惯如统治者般支配群体」相反；后文 once those ruts of procedure are worn into the brain, they're there to stay 也佐证旧习惯不可改变。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"Brain researchers have discovered that the formation of new habits can be____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"predicted."},{"key":"B","text":"regulated."},{"key":"C","text":"traced."},{"key":"D","text":"guided."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"大脑研究人员发现，新习惯的形成可以被____","choicesZh":{"A":"预测","B":"调节","C":"追踪","D":"引导"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Brain researchers have discovered that the formation of new habits can be 是直接复述某项研究的结论，属事实层面的细节复现。","parse":"主句 Brain researchers have discovered，that 引导宾语从句，从句主语 the formation of new habits（of 短语作定语），系动词 + can be + 选项形容词，选项作表语。","locateEn":"But brain researchers have discovered that when we consciously develop new habits, we create parallel paths, and even entirely new brain cells, that can jump our trains of thought onto new, innovative tracks.","locateZh":"但脑科学研究者发现：当我们有意识地培养新习惯时，我们会创造出平行通路，甚至全新的脑细胞，能把我们的思维轨道切换到全新的、富有创造性的轨迹上。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"predicted 意为「可被预测的」，原文从未论及新习惯的形成结果能否被预测，仅强调其形成可由主体主动驱动。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"regulated 含「严格调节、规章约束」之义（如政府监管），原文只说人可有意识地培养（consciously develop），并未上升到「系统化调控」的强度。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"traced 意为「可被追溯/追踪的」，原文谈的是新习惯如何被创造（create parallel paths），并未谈论它能否被追溯。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"「consciously develop」内含「人对习惯形成施加引导」之义，且 P3 的 direct 再次印证；故选 guided。","pairs":[{"orig":"consciously develop new habits","opt":"guided"},{"orig":"we can instead direct our own change by consciously developing new habits","opt":"guided"}]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The word \"ruts\" (Para. 4) is closest in meaning to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tracks."},{"key":"B","text":"series."},{"key":"C","text":"characteristics."},{"key":"D","text":"connections."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"单词\"ruts\"(第4段)在意思上最接近____","choicesZh":{"A":"轨迹","B":"系列","C":"特征","D":"连接"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The word \"ruts\" (Para. 4) is closest in meaning to 是经典词义题句式，明确问 ruts 一词在该语境下的近义词。","parse":"Q23 句子主干：The word \"ruts\" ... is closest in meaning to，(Para. 4) 是定位提示括号，is closest in meaning to 是固定搭配，意为「在意义上最接近于」。","locateEn":"But don't bother trying to kill off old habits; once those ruts of procedure are worn into the brain, they're there to stay. Instead, the new habits we deliberately press into ourselves create parallel pathways that can bypass those old roads.","locateZh":"但别费心去消灭旧习惯了；一旦那些「程序车辙」被磨进大脑，它们就会留在那里。相反，我们刻意压入自己的新习惯会创造出绕过那些旧路的平行通路。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"ruts 字面是「车辙」，在「神经通路」的隐喻语境下与 roads / pathways 等值；四个选项中只有 tracks 具备「路径/轨道」的语义。","pairs":[{"orig":"those old roads","opt":"tracks"},{"orig":"parallel pathways","opt":"tracks"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"series 意为「一系列、序列」，强调线性顺序；ruts 在原文中强调的是「固定路径」而非「顺序排列」，二者语义不同。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"characteristics 意为「特征/特性」，是性质类抽象名词；而 ruts / roads / pathways 都是「通道」类具象名词，二者范畴不同。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"connections 意为「连接/联结」，强调点与点之间的关系；ruts 强调的是「凹陷下去的固定通道」，二者侧重不同——connections 与下文 pathways 的「通路」也不等同。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"Dawna Markova would most probably agree that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ideas are born of a relaxing mind."},{"key":"B","text":"innovativeness could be taught."},{"key":"C","text":"decisiveness derives from fantastic ideas."},{"key":"D","text":"curiosity activates creative minds."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"Dawna Markova很可能会同意____","choicesZh":{"A":"创意源于放松的头脑","B":"创新能力可以被教授","C":"果断源于奇妙的想法","D":"好奇心激活创造性思维"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Dawna Markova would most probably agree that 用「最有可能赞同」明确要求基于其原话作一步推断，而非直接复述。","parse":"Q24 主干 Dawna Markova would most probably agree，that 引导宾语从句，选项整体作 agree 的宾语从句内容。would 表示推测语气，与 most probably 呼应。","locateEn":"\"The first thing needed for innovation is a fascination with wonder,\" says Dawna Markova, author of The Open Mind. ... \"to decide is to kill off all possibilities but one. A good innovational thinker is always exploring the many other possibilities.\"","locateZh":"「创新所需的第一件事是对惊奇的痴迷，」《开放的心智》作者 Dawna Markova 说……「决定就是除一种可能性外杀掉其它所有可能。优秀的创新思考者总是在探索更多可能性。」","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"ideas are born of a relaxing mind 把创新归因于「放松的心智」，但 Markova 谈的是「fascination」（着迷/痴迷），与「放松」相反；段中也无任何关于「放松」状态的论述。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"innovativeness could be taught 意为「创新可被教授」，但 Markova 原话恰恰相反——她在批评 we are taught instead to 'decide'（我们被教成只会决定，而不是探索可能性）；故她不仅没说创新可教，反而暗示当下的教育在压制创新。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"decisiveness derives from fantastic ideas 既把 decisiveness（果断决定）当成被推崇的品质（与原文相反——Markova 批评 decide 是「to kill off all possibilities but one」），又在「果断」与「奇妙想法」之间强加因果（原文无此关系）。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判到「好奇是创新的源头」之后，对照四项：唯有 curiosity activates creative minds 在主语（curiosity）和谓语（activates creative minds）两端都能与 Markova 原话对应，故选 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"a fascination with wonder","opt":"curiosity"},{"orig":"The first thing needed for innovation","opt":"activates creative minds"},{"orig":"A good innovational thinker is always exploring the many other possibilities","opt":"curiosity activates creative minds"}]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Ryan's comments suggest that the practice of standardized testing____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"prevents new habits from being formed."},{"key":"B","text":"no longer emphasizes commonness."},{"key":"C","text":"maintains the inherent American thinking mode."},{"key":"D","text":"complies with the American belief system."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"Ryan的评论表明标准化测试的做法____","choicesZh":{"A":"阻止新习惯的形成","B":"不再强调共性","C":"维持固有的美国思维模式","D":"符合美国的信念体系"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Ryan's comments suggest that the practice of standardized testing 用 suggest 明确要求由 Ryan 的评论推断标准化测试的影响。","parse":"Q25 主干 Ryan's comments suggest，that 引导宾语从句，从句主语是 the practice of standardized testing（of 短语作后置定语），选项整体作从句谓语。","locateEn":"The current emphasis on standardized testing highlights analysis and procedure, meaning that few of us inherently use our innovative and collaborative modes of thought. \"This breaks the major rule in the American belief system – that anyone can do anything,\" explains M. J. Ryan, ... \"That's a lie that we have perpetuated, and it fosters commonness. Knowing what you're good at and doing even more of it creates excellence.\"","locateZh":"当前对标准化测试的强调突出的是分析与程序两种思维，意味着我们当中很少有人会本能地使用自己的创新与协作思维。「这打破了美式信念体系的核心法则——『人人皆可成事』，」M. J. Ryan 解释道……「这是一个我们一直在延续的谎言，它培养出平庸。知道自己擅长什么并把它做得更多，才能造就卓越。」","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"推一步因果：「standardized testing 只激活分析/程序 → 创新/协作被冷落 → 新习惯不易形成」；选项 prevents new habits from being formed 精准接住这条因果链。","pairs":[{"orig":"few of us inherently use our innovative and collaborative modes of thought","opt":"prevents new habits from being formed"},{"orig":"This is where developing new habits comes in.","opt":"prevents new habits from being formed"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"no longer emphasizes commonness 意为「不再强调平庸」，但 Ryan 原话 it fosters commonness 明示标准化测试「正在培养平庸」，与选项极性相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"maintains the inherent American thinking mode 意为「维持了美式固有思维模式」；但 Ryan 原话 This breaks the major rule in the American belief system 用动词 break 明示「打破」，与「maintains」（维持）相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"complies with the American belief system 意为「符合美式信念体系」，但 Ryan 原话 This breaks the major rule in the American belief system 已明示「打破核心法则」——breaks ≠ complies。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"It is a wise father that knows his own child, but today a man can boost his paternal (fatherly) wisdom – or at least confirm that he's the kid's dad. All he needs to do is shell out $30 for a paternity testing kit (PTK) at his local drugstore – and another $120 to get the results."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"More than 60,000 people have purchased the PTKs since they first became available without prescriptions last year, according to Doug Fogg, chief operating officer of Identigene, which makes the over-the-counter kits. More than two dozen companies sell DNA tests directly to the public, ranging in price from a few hundred dollars to more than $2,500."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Among the most popular: paternity and kinship testing, which adopted children can use to find their biological relatives and families can use to track down kids put up for adoption. DNA testing is also the latest rage among passionate genealogists – and supports businesses that offer to search for a family's geographic roots."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Most tests require collecting cells by swabbing saliva in the mouth and sending it to the company for testing. All tests require a potential candidate with whom to compare DNA."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"But some observers are skeptical. \"There's a kind of false precision being hawked by people claiming they are doing ancestry testing,\" says Troy Duster, a New York University sociologist. He notes that each individual has many ancestors – numbering in the hundreds just a few centuries back. Yet most ancestry testing only considers a single lineage, either the Y chromosome inherited through men in a father's line or mitochondrial DNA, which is passed down only from mothers. This DNA can reveal genetic information about only one or two ancestors, even though, for example, just three generations back people also have six other great-grandparents or, four generations back, 14 other great-great-grandparents."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"Critics also argue that commercial genetic testing is only as good as the reference collections to which a sample is compared. Databases used by some companies don't rely on data collected systematically but rather lump together information from different research projects. This means that a DNA database may have a lot of data from some regions and not others, so a person's test results may differ depending on the company that processes the results. In addition, the computer programs a company uses to estimate relationships may be patented and not subject to peer review or outside evaluation."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"In Paragraphs 1 and 2, the text shows PTK's____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"easy availability."},{"key":"B","text":"flexibility in pricing."},{"key":"C","text":"successful promotion."},{"key":"D","text":"popularity with households."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在第1段和第2段中,文章展示了PTK的____","choicesZh":{"A":"易获得性。","B":"定价的灵活性。","C":"成功的推广。","D":"在家庭中的受欢迎程度。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 the text shows PTK's____ 要求从第 1、2 段呈现的客观信息里挑一个关于 PTK 的属性，没有 infer/imply/suggest 等推断信号。","parse":"题干主干 the text shows PTK's____，shows 的宾语是 PTK's 后跟的名词短语（由四个选项补全）。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"All he needs to do is shell out $30 for a paternity testing kit (PTK) at his local drugstore – and another $120 to get the results.","locateZh":"他要做的全部就是花 30 美元在家附近的药店买一盒亲子鉴定试剂盒（PTK），再花 120 美元拿到结果。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判说的“获取门槛低、随手可得”正是 easy availability 的字面含义——drugstore + without prescriptions 两重证据共同指向 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"at his local drugstore","opt":"easy availability"},{"orig":"available without prescriptions","opt":"easy availability"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只给了 30 美元 + 120 美元一种固定价目，没有任何阶梯定价、套餐、可选项的描述；flexibility in pricing 是凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说“6 万多人买过”是一个销量事实，并没有评价这是不是“成功的推广”——promotion 还涉及营销策略、宣传渠道、推广手段，原文一概未提。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说有 6 万多人购买，并未限定这些人是家庭购买、家庭使用，更没有“在家庭中流行（popularity with households）”的语义；households 这个词在原文完全不存在。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"PTK is used to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"locate one's birth place."},{"key":"B","text":"promote genetic research."},{"key":"C","text":"identify parent-child kinship."},{"key":"D","text":"choose children for adoption."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"PTK被用来____","choicesZh":{"A":"定位一个人的出生地。","B":"促进基因研究。","C":"识别亲子关系。","D":"为收养挑选儿童。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 PTK is used to____ 询问 PTK 的具体用途，是直接可在原文中查证的事实信息。","parse":"题干 PTK is used to____ 是被动语态待补全句，空白处需要一个动词原形（与 used to 中的 to 构成不定式），四个选项均为动词短语。结构清晰无陷阱。","locateEn":"It is a wise father that knows his own child, but today a man can boost his paternal (fatherly) wisdom – or at least confirm that he's the kid's dad.","locateZh":"知子莫若父——这话说起来容易；不过如今，一个男人可以提升自己作为父亲的智慧，或者至少能证实自己确实是这孩子的爸爸。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"locate one's birth place 涉及“地理”，而 PTK（paternity testing kit）只查血缘，不查地理；A 选项的语义场是 search for a family's geographic roots 那种祖源/地理项目，已经超出 PTK 本身。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只把 PTK 描绘为面向消费者的商业产品（“shell out $30...at his local drugstore”），从未提到它服务于遗传学研究、推动科研进展。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判“确认父子血缘”与 identify parent-child kinship 在语义上完全等值——动词层等值（confirm↔identify）、宾语层等值（dad/kid↔parent-child kinship），无歧义。","pairs":[{"orig":"confirm that he's the kid's dad","opt":"identify parent-child kinship"},{"orig":"paternity testing kit (PTK)","opt":"identify parent-child kinship"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"choose children for adoption（为收养挑选孩子）是收养前的“挑选行为”，而原文 adopted children can use to find their biological relatives 描述的是“被收养者长大后找亲生家庭”，两者方向相反、动作者不同。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"Skeptical observers believe that ancestry testing fails to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"trace distant ancestors."},{"key":"B","text":"rebuild reliable bloodlines."},{"key":"C","text":"fully use genetic information."},{"key":"D","text":"achieve the claimed accuracy."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"持怀疑态度的观察者认为血统检测未能____","choicesZh":{"A":"追溯远古祖先。","B":"重建可靠的血统。","C":"充分利用基因信息。","D":"达到所声称的准确性。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 ancestry testing fails to____ 中的 fails to 要求把怀疑者的具体批评归纳成“做不到什么”，原文不会有完全对应的句子，需要在定位句基础上做一步语义概括。","parse":"题干 Skeptical observers believe that ancestry testing fails to____ 是 believe that 引导的宾语从句，从句主语是 ancestry testing，谓语 fails to + 动词原形。注意要补的内容只是怀疑者眼中“做不到”的事，而非他们认为它“做了”的事，否则极性会反。","locateEn":"There's a kind of false precision being hawked by people claiming they are doing ancestry testing.","locateZh":"（Troy Duster 说：）那些自称做祖源检测的人，其实在兜售一种虚假的精确性。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文确实说每个人有 numbering in the hundreds just a few centuries back 大量远祖，但怀疑者的核心批评不是“无法追溯远祖”，而是“覆盖的祖先太少导致结果不精确”。A 把现象当结论。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"rebuild reliable bloodlines（重建可靠血脉）在原文没有任何映射；怀疑者批的是“精确性虚假”，从未谈论“重建血脉”这一动作。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项把问题归到“没有充分使用遗传信息”。但原文是说测试方法本身只覆盖单一血脉、注定只能给出关于一两位祖先的信息——是“信息天然只有这么多”，不是“信息被浪费没用足”。两者因果方向不同。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"题干 fails to + 选项 D 的 achieve = 原文 false（达不到），题干的怀疑者 + 选项 D 的 claimed = 原文 claiming（所声称）——四个语义零件严丝合缝。","pairs":[{"orig":"false precision","opt":"achieve the claimed accuracy"},{"orig":"claiming they are doing ancestry testing","opt":"the claimed accuracy"}]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"In the last paragraph, a problem commercial genetic testing faces is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"disorganized data collection."},{"key":"B","text":"overlapping database building."},{"key":"C","text":"excessive sample comparison."},{"key":"D","text":"lack of patent evaluation."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在最后一段中,商业基因检测面临的一个问题是____","choicesZh":{"A":"数据收集无序。","B":"数据库建设重叠。","C":"样本比对过度。","D":"缺乏专利评估。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 a problem commercial genetic testing faces is____ 要求从末段直接抽取一项问题，是对客观信息的摘取，不是推断。","parse":"题干 In the last paragraph, a problem commercial genetic testing faces is____ 主干是 a problem is____，commercial genetic testing faces 是省略关系代词 that 的定语从句，修饰 problem。结构平实无陷阱。","locateEn":"Databases used by some companies don't rely on data collected systematically but rather lump together information from different research projects.","locateZh":"一些公司使用的数据库并不依赖系统性收集的数据，而是把来自不同研究项目的信息胡乱拼凑在一起。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判“数据收集不成体系”与 disorganized data collection 在语义上一一等值——disorganized = 不系统 + 胡乱拼凑，data collection = 数据收集。","pairs":[{"orig":"don't rely on data collected systematically","opt":"disorganized data collection"},{"orig":"lump together information from different research projects","opt":"disorganized data collection"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"overlapping（重叠）暗指多个数据库之间有共同条目；原文说的是数据库“有的地区数据多有的少”（a lot of data from some regions and not others），是覆盖不均，不是数据库间互相重叠。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说商业基因检测的好坏取决于参考数据库，并未说“样本比对得太多”。excessive（过度）这一程度词在原文找不到任何支持。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文末句 the computer programs a company uses to estimate relationships may be patented and not subject to peer review or outside evaluation 说的是“算法已申请专利、因此不接受同行评议或外部评估”——缺的是“对算法本身的外部评估”，不是“对专利的评估”。D 把宾语换错了。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"An appropriate title for the text is most likely to be____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Fors and Againsts of DNA Testing."},{"key":"B","text":"DNA Testing and Its Problems."},{"key":"C","text":"DNA Testing Outside the Lab."},{"key":"D","text":"Lies Behind DNA Testing."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"这篇文章最合适的标题可能是____","choicesZh":{"A":"DNA检测的正反方观点。","B":"DNA检测及其问题。","C":"实验室外的DNA检测。","D":"DNA检测背后的谎言。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 An appropriate title for the text is most likely to be____ 直接要求选最合适的标题，是主旨题中的标题款。","parse":"题干 An appropriate title for the text is most likely to be____ 主干为 An appropriate title is____，most likely to be 是表语前的弱化语气短语，提示“最可能”——四选一里选最贴的，不必百分百完美。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Fors and Againsts（赞成与反对）要求文章里有明确支持 DNA 检测的一方立论；本文除了中性介绍商业现状，没有任何“支持/赞成”派的正面论证，只有“中性介绍 + 批评”两半，“Fors”那一半空缺。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项中 DNA Testing 罩住前半的介绍区间（PTK、亲子、祖源、商业检测），Its Problems 罩住后半的怀疑者与批评者两段——这正是预判要求的“两半同时覆盖”，且字面与语义都最贴。","pairs":[{"orig":"false precision","opt":"DNA Testing and Its Problems"},{"orig":"Critics also argue that commercial genetic testing is only as good as the reference collections","opt":"DNA Testing and Its Problems"},{"orig":"a paternity testing kit (PTK)","opt":"DNA Testing"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Outside the Lab（在实验室之外）只能描述“DNA 检测走出实验室、走向普通消费者”这一现象，仅覆盖前半（P1 P2 的药店销售）的氛围；对 P5 P6 两段批评毫无承载，主旨严重缩水。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Lies（谎言/欺骗）暗示“刻意欺瞒”的强否定立场；原文怀疑者用的是 false precision、批评者用的是 don't rely on...systematically，都是指“做得不好/不严谨”，没有指控“故意撒谎”。D 把作者中性引述的批评升级成了“揭露骗局”的强否定调性。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"The relationship between formal education and economic growth in poor countries is widely misunderstood by economists and politicians alike. Progress in both areas is undoubtedly necessary for the social, political, and intellectual development of these and all other societies; however, the conventional view that education should be one of the very highest priorities for promoting rapid economic development in poor countries is wrong. We are fortunate that it is, because building new educational systems there and putting enough people through them to improve economic performance would require two or three generations. The findings of a research institution have consistently shown that workers in all countries can be trained on the job to achieve radically higher productivity and, as a result, radically higher standards of living."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"Ironically, the first evidence for this idea appeared in the United States. Not long ago, with the country entering a recession and Japan at its pre-bubble peak, the U.S. workforce was derided as poorly educated and one of the primary causes of the poor U.S. economic performance. Japan was, and remains, the global leader in automotive-assembly productivity. Yet the research revealed that the U.S. factories of Honda, Nissan, and Toyota achieved about 95 percent of the productivity of their Japanese counterparts – a result of the training that U.S. workers received on the job."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"More recently, while examining housing construction, the researchers discovered that illiterate, non-English-speaking Mexican workers in Houston, Texas, consistently met best-practice labor productivity standards despite the complexity of the building industry's work."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"What is the real relationship between education and economic development? We have to suspect that continuing economic growth promotes the development of education even when governments don't force it. After all, that's how education got started. When our ancestors were hunters and gatherers 10,000 years ago, they didn't have time to wonder much about anything besides finding food. Only when humanity began to get its food in a more productive way was there time for other things."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"As education improved, humanity's productivity potential increased as well. When the competitive environment pushed our ancestors to achieve that potential, they could in turn afford more education. This increasingly high level of education is probably a necessary, but not a sufficient, condition for the complex political systems required by advanced economic performance. Thus poor countries might not be able to escape their poverty traps without political changes that may be possible only with broader formal education. A lack of formal education, however, doesn't constrain the ability of the developing world's workforce to substantially improve productivity for the foreseeable future. On the contrary, constraints on improving productivity explain why education isn't developing more quickly there than it is."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The author holds in Paragraph 1 that the importance of education in poor countries____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is subject to groundless doubts."},{"key":"B","text":"has fallen victim of bias."},{"key":"C","text":"is conventionally downgraded."},{"key":"D","text":"has been overestimated."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者在第一段中认为教育在贫穷国家的重要性____","choicesZh":{"A":"受到毫无根据的质疑。","B":"已沦为偏见的牺牲品。","C":"通常被低估。","D":"被高估了。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author holds in Paragraph 1 that the importance of education in poor countries 限定段落、问作者对一个话题的看法，答案应能在段内直接读出。","parse":"The author holds in Paragraph 1 that the importance of education in poor countries____ 是不完整陈述句，选项是它的延续；主干 The author holds that...，that 从句的主语是 the importance of education in poor countries，谓语在四个选项里。无陷阱。","locateEn":"however, the conventional view that education should be one of the very highest priorities for promoting rapid economic development in poor countries is wrong.","locateZh":"然而，那种认为教育应当是穷国推动快速经济发展的最高优先事项之一的传统看法是错误的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"作者只说传统观点错，并未说有人对教育的重要性提出 groundless doubts，更未评价这些怀疑是否无根据。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"作者驳的是「传统观点」，并未把这种观点定性为偏见，更没说教育「fall victim of bias」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 education should be one of the very highest priorities 显示传统观点是把教育看得「高」，C 项却说 is conventionally downgraded（按传统被低估），方向反了。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判说「教育被高估」，四个选项里只有 has been overestimated 直接对应此语义，无需推理跳跃。","pairs":[{"orig":"the conventional view that education should be one of the very highest priorities for promoting rapid economic development in poor countries is wrong","opt":"has been overestimated"}]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"It is stated in Paragraph 1 that the construction of a new educational system____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"challenges economists and politicians."},{"key":"B","text":"takes efforts of generations."},{"key":"C","text":"demands priority from the government."},{"key":"D","text":"requires sufficient labor force."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第一段指出,构建新的教育体系____","choicesZh":{"A":"对经济学家和政治家构成挑战。","B":"需要几代人的努力。","C":"需要政府优先考虑。","D":"需要充足的劳动力。"},"analysis":{"type":"It is stated in Paragraph 1 that 含 stated 且锁段，属于段内事实陈述题。","parse":"It is stated in Paragraph 1 that the construction of a new educational system____ 形式主语 It，真正主语是 that 从句；从句主语 the construction of a new educational system，谓语在选项里。无陷阱。","locateEn":"We are fortunate that it is, because building new educational systems there and putting enough people through them to improve economic performance would require two or three generations.","locateZh":"我们是幸运的，因为在那些国家建设新的教育系统并让足够多的人接受教育以提升经济表现，会需要两三代人的时间。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"作者只说经济学家和政治家「误解」教育与经济的关系，widely misunderstood by economists and politicians alike，并不是说新教育系统的建设本身在挑战他们。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项中只有 takes efforts of generations 与「two or three generations」直接对应，预判与选项一一锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"would require two or three generations","opt":"takes efforts of generations"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"作者主张教育不该被列为穷国最高优先级，the conventional view that education should be one of the very highest priorities ... is wrong，C 项却说新建教育系统「要求政府优先」，正好反了。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 putting enough people through them 强调「让足够多的人受完教育」是花费时间的方式，而非把「足够劳动力」当作建设新系统的前提条件。D 项把语义偷成「需要充足劳动力」。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"A major difference between the Japanese and U.S. workforces is that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the Japanese workforce is better disciplined."},{"key":"B","text":"the Japanese workforce is more productive."},{"key":"C","text":"the U.S. workforce has a better education."},{"key":"D","text":"the U.S. workforce is more organized."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"日本劳动力与美国劳动力的一个主要区别是____","choicesZh":{"A":"日本劳动力纪律性更好。","B":"日本劳动力生产效率更高。","C":"美国劳动力受教育程度更高。","D":"美国劳动力组织性更强。"},"analysis":{"type":"A major difference between the Japanese and U.S. workforces is that____ 问的是两国劳动力之间一个可在文中读出的客观差异。","parse":"A major difference between the Japanese and U.S. workforces is that____ 主干为 A difference is that...，is 后的 that 从句被选项补完；between... 介词短语作 difference 的后置定语。无陷阱。","locateEn":"Japan was, and remains, the global leader in automotive-assembly productivity.","locateZh":"日本（当时）是、现在仍然是汽车装配生产率领域的全球领头羊。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文都在谈「生产率、培训、教育」，没有任何句子涉及日本工人「更守纪律」better disciplined。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项里只有 the Japanese workforce is more productive 直接谈生产率高低，与预判一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"Japan was, and remains, the global leader in automotive-assembly productivity","opt":"the Japanese workforce is more productive"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 the U.S. workforce was derided as poorly educated 明说美国工人被讥为受教育差，C 项却说 the U.S. workforce has a better education，方向反了。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文未提及任何一方工人的「组织程度」more organized，这一评价维度全无依据。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"The author quotes the example of our ancestors to show that education emerged____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"when people had enough time."},{"key":"B","text":"prior to better ways of finding food."},{"key":"C","text":"when people no longer went hungry."},{"key":"D","text":"as a result of pressure on government."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者引用我们祖先的例子来说明教育出现于____","choicesZh":{"A":"人们有足够时间的时候。","B":"寻找食物的更好方法之前。","C":"人们不再挨饿的时候。","D":"政府面临压力的结果。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author quotes the example of our ancestors to show that 含 quote the example...to show，标准的例证目的题问法。","parse":"The author quotes the example of our ancestors to show that education emerged____ 主干为 The author quotes ... to show that...；to show 是目的状语；that 从句被选项延续。无陷阱。","locateEn":"When our ancestors were hunters and gatherers 10,000 years ago, they didn't have time to wonder much about anything besides finding food. Only when humanity began to get its food in a more productive way was there time for other things.","locateZh":"当一万年前我们的祖先还是狩猎采集者时，他们除了找食物之外没有时间去琢磨别的事情。只有当人类开始以更高效的方式获取食物时，才有时间去做其他事情。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判直接指向「有时间是教育出现的前提」，A 项 when people had enough time 是这一前提的字面表达，无须推理。","pairs":[{"orig":"Only when humanity began to get its food in a more productive way was there time for other things","opt":"when people had enough time"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文先说更高效的获取食物方式，才有时间做其他事；选项 prior to better ways of finding food 却把教育放在「更好的找食物方式」之前，因果与先后被颠倒。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说「以更高效方式获取食物」给出了余暇，并未说人们「不再挨饿」no longer went hungry——「高效获取」≠「彻底解决饥饿」，C 把程度推得更远。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全段没有出现政府或对政府的压力；作者只说生产率提升带出余暇，与 pressure on government 毫无关系。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"According to the last paragraph, development of education____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"results directly from competitive environments."},{"key":"B","text":"does not depend on economic performance."},{"key":"C","text":"follows improved productivity."},{"key":"D","text":"cannot afford political changes."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据最后一段,教育的发展____","choicesZh":{"A":"直接源于竞争环境。","B":"不依赖于经济表现。","C":"跟随生产力的提高。","D":"无法承受政治变革。"},"analysis":{"type":"According to the last paragraph, development of education____ 含 according to + 段落，属段内事实题。","parse":"According to the last paragraph, development of education____ According to... 是状语；主语是 development of education，谓语在选项中。无陷阱。","locateEn":"As education improved, humanity's productivity potential increased as well. When the competitive environment pushed our ancestors to achieve that potential, they could in turn afford more education. ... constraints on improving productivity explain why education isn't developing more quickly there than it is.","locateZh":"随着教育改善，人类的生产潜能也随之提高。当竞争环境促使祖先把这种潜能转化为现实生产率后，他们反过来才负担得起更多教育。……是生产率改善受到约束，解释了那些国家教育为什么发展不快。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 When the competitive environment pushed our ancestors to achieve that potential, they could in turn afford more education 中，competitive environment 直接作用于生产率潜能的实现，再「反过来」（in turn）才促成教育；A 项 results directly from competitive environments 把竞争环境写成教育发展的「直接」原因，跳过了「生产率」这一中介。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"末段全段都在强调教育发展依赖生产率（经济表现）的改善，constraints on improving productivity explain why education isn't developing more quickly 直接把教育发展归因于生产率；B 项却说教育发展 does not depend on economic performance，方向反了。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"follow 一词直接表达「跟随、随之而来」，正是预判中「教育发展在生产率提升之后」的字面表达。","pairs":[{"orig":"they could in turn afford more education","opt":"follows improved productivity"},{"orig":"constraints on improving productivity explain why education isn't developing more quickly there than it is","opt":"follows improved productivity"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 they could in turn afford more education 说人们「负担得起教育」，并未说教育「负担不起政治变革」cannot afford political changes——afford 的主语和宾语都被换。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"The most thoroughly studied intellectuals in the history of the New World are the ministers and political leaders of seventeenth-century New England. According to the standard history of American philosophy, nowhere else in colonial America was \"so much importance attached to intellectual pursuits.\" According to many books and articles, New England's leaders established the basic themes and preoccupations of an unfolding, dominant Puritan tradition in American intellectual life."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"To take this approach to the New Englanders normally means to start with the Puritans' theological innovations and their distinctive ideas about the church – important subjects that we may not neglect. But in keeping with our examination of southern intellectual life, we may consider the original Puritans as carriers of European culture, adjusting to New World circumstances. The New England colonies were the scenes of important episodes in the pursuit of widely understood ideals of civility and virtuosity."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"The early settlers of Massachusetts Bay included men of impressive education and influence in England. Besides the ninety or so learned ministers who came to Massachusetts churches in the decade after 1629, there were political leaders like John Winthrop, an educated gentleman, lawyer, and official of the Crown before he journeyed to Boston. These men wrote and published extensively, reaching both New World and Old World audiences, and giving New England an atmosphere of intellectual earnestness."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"We should not forget, however, that most New Englanders were less well educated. While few craftsmen or farmers, let alone dependents and servants, left literary compositions to be analyzed, it is obvious that their views were less fully intellectualized. Their thinking often had a traditional superstitious quality. A tailor named John Dane, who emigrated in the late 1630s, left an account of his reasons for leaving England that is filled with signs. Sexual confusion, economic frustrations, and religious hope – all came together in a decisive moment when he opened the Bible, told his father that the first line he saw would settle his fate, and read the magical words: \"Come out from among them, touch no unclean thing, and I will be your God and you shall be my people.\" One wonders what Dane thought of the careful sermons explaining the Bible that he heard in Puritan churches."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Meanwhile, many settlers had slighter religious commitments than Dane's, as one clergyman learned in confronting folk along the coast who mocked that they had not come to the New World for religion. \"Our main end was to catch fish.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"The author holds that in the seventeenth-century New England____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Puritan tradition dominated political life."},{"key":"B","text":"intellectual interests were encouraged."},{"key":"C","text":"politics benefited much from intellectual endeavors."},{"key":"D","text":"intellectual pursuits enjoyed a liberal environment."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者认为在十七世纪的新英格兰____","choicesZh":{"A":"清教传统主导了政治生活。","B":"知识兴趣受到鼓励。","C":"政治从知识努力中获益良多。","D":"知识追求享有自由的环境。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author holds that in the seventeenth-century New England____是个待补全的陈述句，不含 infer/imply/mainly about，属于对作者明确表达的客观信息做选择。","parse":"The author holds that in the seventeenth-century New England____是个『主句 + that 宾语从句』的待补全句；空位接的是宾语从句的谓语部分，意思要补成『作者认为 17 世纪新英格兰<怎么样>』，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"According to the standard history of American philosophy, nowhere else in colonial America was \"so much importance attached to intellectual pursuits.\"","locateZh":"据美国哲学的标准史所述，在殖民地时期的美洲，没有任何别的地方对知识追求给予如此之多的重视。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Puritan tradition dominated political life中『dominated political life（主导政治生活）』在第 1 段完全没有依据；原文只说清教传统主导了智识/思想生活dominant Puritan tradition in American intellectual life，不是政治生活。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判的『知识追求受高度重视』几乎一一对应到intellectual interests were encouraged，无需推断、最稳妥。","pairs":[{"orig":"so much importance attached to intellectual pursuits","opt":"intellectual interests were encouraged"},{"orig":"intellectual pursuits","opt":"intellectual interests"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"politics benefited much from intellectual endeavors中『政治从知识努力中获益良多』在首段没有任何对应表述，作者只谈对知识追求的重视，未谈两者间的受益关系。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"intellectual pursuits enjoyed a liberal environment把『被重视』升级成『享有自由宽松的环境』，原文只有『被重视』而没说『自由』，属于过度推断。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"It is suggested in Paragraph 2 that New Englanders____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"experienced a comparatively peaceful early history."},{"key":"B","text":"brought with them the culture of the Old World."},{"key":"C","text":"paid little attention to southern intellectual life."},{"key":"D","text":"were obsessed with religious innovations."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第2段暗示新英格兰人____","choicesZh":{"A":"经历了相对和平的早期历史。","B":"带来了旧世界的文化。","C":"很少关注南方的知识生活。","D":"痴迷于宗教革新。"},"analysis":{"type":"It is suggested in Paragraph 2 that New Englanders____问的是段落里所建议/说明的内容，虽含 suggested 但被锁定在某段，仍按段内事实题处理。","parse":"It is suggested in Paragraph 2 that New Englanders____是『it is + 过去分词 + that 从句』的形式主语结构，真正主语是 that 从句；空位补的是 New Englanders 的谓语，要找第 2 段中对新英格兰人的核心定性。","locateEn":"But in keeping with our examination of southern intellectual life, we may consider the original Puritans as carriers of European culture, adjusting to New World circumstances.","locateZh":"不过，与我们对南方知识生活的考察相一致，我们可以把最初的清教徒视为欧洲文化的承载者，他们在新世界的环境中加以调整。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"experienced a comparatively peaceful early history中『相对平和的早期历史』在第 2 段没有任何表达，段内谈的是文化承载与调整，不是历史氛围。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判中的『把欧洲文化带过来』与brought with them the culture of the Old World在动作主体、动作内容、对象上完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"carriers of European culture","opt":"brought with them the culture of the Old World"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文是『与南方知识生活的考察保持一致』in keeping with our examination of southern intellectual life，意思是作者的研究方法和南方对齐；选项paid little attention to southern intellectual life却说『几乎不关注南方知识生活』，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"段中提到清教徒的神学创新等是important subjects that we may not neglect，意思是不应忽视，并不等于『沉迷/痴迷』；选项were obsessed with religious innovations中 obsessed 程度过重。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"The early ministers and political leaders in Massachusetts Bay____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were famous in the New World for their writings."},{"key":"B","text":"gained increasing importance in religious affairs."},{"key":"C","text":"abandoned high positions before coming to the New World."},{"key":"D","text":"created a new intellectual atmosphere in New England."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"马萨诸塞湾的早期牧师和政治领袖____","choicesZh":{"A":"因其著作在新世界闻名。","B":"在宗教事务中日益重要。","C":"在来到新世界之前放弃了高位。","D":"在新英格兰创造了一种新的知识氛围。"},"analysis":{"type":"The early ministers and political leaders in Massachusetts Bay____待补全句，问『这群人具体做了什么』，是对文段客观陈述的复述选择。","parse":"The early ministers and political leaders in Massachusetts Bay____主语是由 and 并列的两类人，谓语就是要补的空；理解时把两类人合在一起当一个主语处理即可，无陷阱。","locateEn":"These men wrote and published extensively, reaching both New World and Old World audiences, and giving New England an atmosphere of intellectual earnestness.","locateZh":"这些人著述并出版甚丰，受众覆盖新旧两大陆，并赋予新英格兰一种知识严肃认真的气氛。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文说他们的著作reaching both New World and Old World audiences，影响及于新旧两大陆；选项were famous in the New World for their writings只说在新世界出名，把影响范围缩到一半，且 famous 也无原文明文依据，属以偏概全。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"gained increasing importance in religious affairs中『在宗教事务中重要性日益增加』在第 3 段没有任何对应；段中只谈他们著述影响和智识氛围，没说他们在宗教中地位变化。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文说 John Winthropan educated gentleman, lawyer, and official of the Crown before he journeyed to Boston，说明他来新世界之前担任王室官员；并未说他『放弃高位』，文段只交代身份并未说他放弃。选项abandoned high positions before coming to the New World强加 abandoned 这一动作。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判中的『营造出新英格兰的智识氛围』完全对应created a new intellectual atmosphere in New England。","pairs":[{"orig":"giving New England an atmosphere of intellectual earnestness","opt":"created a new intellectual atmosphere in New England"},{"orig":"wrote and published extensively","opt":"created a new intellectual atmosphere in New England"}]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"The story of John Dane shows that less well-educated New Englanders were often____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"influenced by superstitions."},{"key":"B","text":"troubled with religious beliefs."},{"key":"C","text":"puzzled by church sermons."},{"key":"D","text":"frustrated with family earnings."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"约翰·丹恩的故事表明受教育程度较低的新英格兰人常常____","choicesZh":{"A":"受到迷信的影响。","B":"为宗教信仰所困扰。","C":"对教堂布道感到困惑。","D":"对家庭收入感到沮丧。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干The story of John Dane shows that明示 Dane 的故事是论据，问的是它『证明了什么』，是典型的『例子→论点』题。","parse":"The story of John Dane shows that less well-educated New Englanders were often____主语是 The story of John Dane，谓语 shows 引出宾语从句；从句主语是受教育较少的新英格兰人，谓语 were often 后接空白，要补的是该群体的常见特征，注意 often 暗示这是共性而非个例。","locateEn":"Their thinking often had a traditional superstitious quality. A tailor named John Dane, who emigrated in the late 1630s, left an account of his reasons for leaving England that is filled with signs.","locateZh":"他们的思想往往带有传统的迷信色彩。一位叫 John Dane 的裁缝在 1630 年代晚期移民，他留下了一份关于自己离开英格兰原因的记述，其中充满了各种预兆。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判中的『迷信色彩』直接对应 A 项的 superstitions，例子和论点双重支撑，A 最稳。","pairs":[{"orig":"Their thinking often had a traditional superstitious quality","opt":"influenced by superstitions"},{"orig":"filled with signs","opt":"influenced by superstitions"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文说Sexual confusion, economic frustrations, and religious hope——宗教是 hope（希望），不是 troubled（困扰）；选项troubled with religious beliefs在情感方向上与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"段末One wonders what Dane thought of the careful sermons explaining the Bible that he heard in Puritan churches是作者本人在好奇/揣测 Dane 对布道的看法，并不等于 Dane 本人被布道弄糊涂；选项puzzled by church sermons张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文是economic frustrations——泛指经济上的挫折；选项frustrated with family earnings把它具体化为『家庭收入』，偷换了概念范围；且 family earnings 也不是文本所言。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"The text suggests that early settlers in New England____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"were mostly engaged in political activities."},{"key":"B","text":"were motivated by an illusory prospect."},{"key":"C","text":"came from different intellectual backgrounds."},{"key":"D","text":"left few formal records for later reference."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"文章表明新英格兰的早期定居者____","choicesZh":{"A":"大多从事政治活动。","B":"受到虚幻前景的驱使。","C":"来自不同的知识背景。","D":"为后人留下的正式记录很少。"},"analysis":{"type":"The text suggests that early settlers in New England____要求对全文谈到的早期定居者做整体归纳，主语 the text + 全文性话题双重信号锁定主旨题。","parse":"The text suggests that early settlers in New England____是『主语 + suggests + that 宾语从句』结构，从句主语 early settlers in New England 接待补谓语；意思上要补『文章暗示这些定居者<整体上是怎样的>』，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"were mostly engaged in political activities中『大多从事政治活动』只能对应第 3 段中的政治领袖部分，无法覆盖第 4 段工匠/农民和第 5 段渔民；且 mostly 在原文也无依据。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"were motivated by an illusory prospect中『被一种虚幻的前景驱动』是负面评价；原文虽提到religious hope，但作者未将其定性为『虚幻』，第 5 段中 catch fish 更是实在的世俗动机，与 illusory 相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 是唯一能同时覆盖第 3、4、5 段三类人的归纳；其它选项要么只覆盖某一段，要么与原文不符。","pairs":[{"orig":"These men wrote and published extensively","opt":"came from different intellectual backgrounds"},{"orig":"Their thinking often had a traditional superstitious quality","opt":"came from different intellectual backgrounds"},{"orig":"Our main end was to catch fish","opt":"came from different intellectual backgrounds"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文是While few craftsmen or farmers, let alone dependents and servants, left literary compositions to be analyzed，只说工匠和农民等基层人留下的文字少，并未说全体早期定居者『几乎没留下正式记录』；第 3 段明确说牧师和政治领袖wrote and published extensively，与 D 项相矛盾。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"matching","title":"Section II Part B 选句填空","directions":"Directions: In the following text, some segments have been removed. For Questions 41-45, choose the most suitable one from the list A-G to fit into each of the numbered blanks. There are two extra choices, which do not fit in any of the blanks. Mark your answers on ANSWER SHEET 1. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"Coinciding with the groundbreaking theory of biological evolution proposed by British naturalist Charles Darwin in the 1860s, British social philosopher Herbert Spencer put forward his own theory of biological and cultural evolution. Spencer argued that all worldly phenomena, including human societies, changed over time, advancing toward perfection. {{41}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"American social scientist Lewis Henry Morgan introduced another theory of cultural evolution in the late 1800s. Morgan helped found modern anthropology – the scientific study of human societies, customs and beliefs – thus becoming one of the earliest anthropologists. In his work, he attempted to show how all aspects of culture changed together in the evolution of societies. {{42}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"In the early 1900s in North America, German-born American anthropologist Franz Boas developed a new theory of culture known as historical particularism. Historical particularism, which emphasized the uniqueness of all cultures, gave new direction to anthropology. {{43}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"Boas felt that the culture of any society must be understood as the result of a unique history and not as one of many cultures belonging to a broader evolutionary stage or type of culture. {{44}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"Historical particularism became a dominant approach to the study of culture in American anthropology, largely through the influence of many students of Boas. But a number of anthropologists in the early 1900s also rejected the particularist theory of culture in favor of diffusionism. Some attributed virtually every important cultural achievement to the inventions of a few, especially gifted peoples that, according to diffusionists, then spread to other cultures. {{45}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"Also in the early 1900s, French sociologist Émile Durkheim developed a theory of culture that would greatly influence anthropology. Durkheim proposed that religious beliefs functioned to reinforce social solidarity. An interest in the relationship between the function of society and culture became a major theme in European, and especially British, anthropology."}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy."},{"key":"C","text":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies."},{"key":"D","text":"They also focused on important rituals that appeared to preserve a people's social structure, such as initiation ceremonies that formally signify children's entrance into adulthood."},{"key":"E","text":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved."},{"key":"F","text":"Supporters of the theory viewed culture as a collection of integrated parts that work together to keep a society functioning."},{"key":"G","text":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy."},{"key":"C","text":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies."},{"key":"D","text":"They also focused on important rituals that appeared to preserve a people's social structure, such as initiation ceremonies that formally signify children's entrance into adulthood."},{"key":"E","text":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved."},{"key":"F","text":"Supporters of the theory viewed culture as a collection of integrated parts that work together to keep a society functioning."},{"key":"G","text":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"段末","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies. 他认为人类进化的特点是一种他称之为\"适者生存\"的斗争,在这种斗争中,较弱的种族和社会最终必然被更强大、更先进的种族和社会所取代。\n承接 Spencer「万物向完善前进」，补一句他进化论的具体内容 空前一句是 Spencer argued that all worldly phenomena, including human societies, changed over time, advancing toward perfection——交代了 Spencer 进化论的总纲：万物随时间向完善发展。第1段到此结束，第2段另起讲 Morgan。因此这个段末空要补一句继续展开 Spencer 进化思想的话，把「向完善前进」具体化为他理论的某个核心命题。\nHe 承指 Spencer + survival of the fittest 把「向完善前进」机制化，逐条对上 句首 He argued 的 He 在上文唯一落实为 Herbert Spencer，代词有着落；survival of the fittest 与 weaker … replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies 正是把空前句 advancing toward perfection 的笼统说法机制化——弱者被强者、更先进者取代，话题词同向复现。结构上它续讲 Spencer、不抢下段 Morgan 的戏，段末延展功能也对上。三类线索全中。","options":{},"choiceEn":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies.","clues":["结构功能 段末位置 + 下段换主角，定本空为 Spencer 进化论的延展句 本空处在第1段末 advancing toward perfection. __(41)__，其后第2段开头另起 American social scientist Lewis Henry Morgan introduced another theory。结构上本空夹在「Spencer 总纲」与「下一位学者登场」之间，要求正确句仍在讲 Spencer 的进化主张，是对上文的延展，而非转向新人。","词汇复现 advancing toward perfection 呼应「由弱到强、更先进」的进化措辞 空前句 changed over time, advancing toward perfection 给出「随时间向更高级发展」的语义，正确句应复现这一进化逻辑——出现「更强、更先进」「被取代／淘汰」一类与「向完善前进」同向的措辞，把 Spencer 笼统的进化观落到一个具体机制上。","代词指代 正确句宜用 He 承指上文唯一男性学者 Spencer 本段主语自始至终是 Herbert Spencer 一人，正确句若以 He 开头主张某观点，这个 He 能顺势在上文找到唯一先行词 Spencer，衔接自然；据此正确句很可能是一句以 He 引导的、陈述 Spencer 进一步主张的话。"]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy."},{"key":"C","text":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies."},{"key":"D","text":"They also focused on important rituals that appeared to preserve a people's social structure, such as initiation ceremonies that formally signify children's entrance into adulthood."},{"key":"E","text":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved."},{"key":"F","text":"Supporters of the theory viewed culture as a collection of integrated parts that work together to keep a society functioning."},{"key":"G","text":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world."}],"answer":"E","explanation":{"answer":"E","type":"段末","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved. 因此,在他看来,文化的各个方面,如家庭结构、婚姻形式、亲属关系类别、财产所有权、政府形式、技术以及食物生产体系,都随着社会的演化而改变。\n承接 Morgan「展示文化各方面如何共同变化」，补一句把这点铺开的总结 空前句是 he attempted to show how all aspects of culture changed together in the evolution of societies，点明 Morgan 理论的核心命题：文化所有方面在社会进化中一同变化。第2段到此结束，第3段另起讲 Boas。因此本段末空要补一句对 Morgan 这一命题的展开或总结，把「各方面一同变化」具体化或收束。\nThus 承推论 + diverse aspects of culture…all changed 复现前句，逐条吻合 Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture … all changed as societies evolved 句首 Thus 紧承前句命题作推论；his 在上文唯一落实为 Lewis Henry Morgan；diverse aspects of culture、all changed as societies evolved 与空前句 all aspects of culture changed together in the evolution of societies 几乎逐词复现，并把抽象的 all aspects 用 families、marriage、kinship 等清单坐实。逻辑、代词、词汇三类线索全中。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved.","clues":["词汇复现 all aspects of culture changed together 在正确句应再次出现 空前句 all aspects of culture changed together in the evolution of societies 是本空的核心复现锚点，正确句应再次提到「文化的各个方面」「随社会演进一起变化」这一组词，把抽象的 all aspects 列举或重申一遍。","逻辑连接 前句给出命题，本空宜用「因此」承接作推论/展开 空前句 he attempted to show how all aspects of culture changed together 是 Morgan 想论证的命题，本空与它构成「提出命题 → 因此其各方面如何如何」的推论关系，要求正确句带 Thus／因此 一类承上推论的连接词。","代词指代 正确句宜用 his 承指本段唯一男性学者 Morgan 本段主角是 Lewis Henry Morgan 一人，正确句若用 in his view 一类说法陈述「他的观点」，这个 his 能在上文唯一落实为 Morgan，衔接顺畅；据此正确句很可能含一个指代 Morgan 的 his。"]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy."},{"key":"C","text":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies."},{"key":"D","text":"They also focused on important rituals that appeared to preserve a people's social structure, such as initiation ceremonies that formally signify children's entrance into adulthood."},{"key":"E","text":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved."},{"key":"F","text":"Supporters of the theory viewed culture as a collection of integrated parts that work together to keep a society functioning."},{"key":"G","text":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"段末","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism. 其他人类学家认为文化革新,如发明创造,具有单一起源并在不同社会之间传播。这一理论被称为传播论。\nBoas 历史特殊论已登场，本空补一句承上启下、引出与之并列/对立的另一群人 空前句是 Historical particularism, which emphasized the uniqueness of all cultures, gave new direction to anthropology——交代 Boas 的历史特殊论强调文化独特性、给人类学指出新方向。第3段到此结束，第4段开头 Boas felt that the culture of any society must be understood as the result of a unique history 仍在讲 Boas。本段末空要补一句承上的话：既呼应上文学派之争的格局，又能为后文铺垫。\nOther anthropologists 引出对立群体 + This theory was known as diffusionism 命名，逐条对上 Other anthropologists believed 的 Other 紧承上文历史特殊论，引出持不同主张的另一群人，逻辑对照成立；This theory was known as diffusionism 正式给该理论命名，恰好为第5段 rejected the particularist theory of culture in favor of diffusionism 的展开埋下名号，结构上的命名/承启功能完全吻合。逻辑连接与结构功能两类线索全中。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism.","clues":["逻辑连接 上文立起历史特殊论，本空宜用 Other 引出对立的另一群人 空前句 Historical particularism, which emphasized the uniqueness of all cultures 立起一种鲜明立场，本空与它构成对照关系，要求正确句带 Other／另一些 一类标记，引出与历史特殊论持不同主张的另一群人类学家。","结构功能 本空要为后文「扩散论」埋名，是引出新理论的命名句 后文第5段反复出现 rejected the particularist theory of culture in favor of diffusionism，说明扩散论是与历史特殊论对立的关键概念。本空处在该对立正式展开之前，结构上承担「点出并命名这一对立理论」的功能，正确句应是给某个理论命名（…was known as…）的总起句。"]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy."},{"key":"C","text":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies."},{"key":"D","text":"They also focused on important rituals that appeared to preserve a people's social structure, such as initiation ceremonies that formally signify children's entrance into adulthood."},{"key":"E","text":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved."},{"key":"F","text":"Supporters of the theory viewed culture as a collection of integrated parts that work together to keep a society functioning."},{"key":"G","text":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"段末","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy. 为了尽可能完整地研究特定文化,他精通语言学(对语言的研究)和体质人类学(对人类生物学和解剖学的研究)。\n承接 Boas「文化须作为独特历史的结果来理解」，补一句他为此采取的研究做法 空前句是 Boas felt that the culture of any society must be understood as the result of a unique history and not as one of many cultures belonging to a broader evolutionary stage——讲 Boas 主张每个文化要作为其独特历史的结果来理解。第4段到此结束，第5段另起讲历史特殊论的传播与扩散论。本段末空要补一句顺着 Boas 这一主张往下、说明他为落实「研究独特文化」而具体怎么做的话。\nhe 承指 Boas + particular cultures 复现独特性 + 给出具体研究做法，逐条对上 he became skilled in linguistics … and in physical anthropology 的 he 在上文唯一落实为 Boas；study particular cultures as completely as possible 的 particular 复现 a unique history、the uniqueness of all cultures 的独特性主题；内容上它正是 Boas 为贯彻「按独特历史理解文化」而采取的具体做法（精通语言学、体质人类学）。代词、词汇、结构功能三类线索全中。","options":{},"choiceEn":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy.","clues":["代词指代 正确句的 he 须承指本段唯一男性学者 Boas 第4段主角是 Boas 一人（以 he 行文），正确句若以 he 陈述「他做了什么」，这个 he 能在上文唯一落实为 Boas；据此正确句很可能含一个指代 Boas 的 he。","词汇复现 a unique history / uniqueness 与正确句 particular cultures 同义呼应 空前句 the result of a unique history 与本段所属理论 emphasized the uniqueness of all cultures 都强调「独特／特定」，正确句应复现这一语义——出现 particular cultures 一类说法，表明它要讲的正是 Boas 为研究「特定文化」而采取的手段。"]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Other anthropologists believed that cultural innovations, such as inventions, had a single origin and passed from society to society. This theory was known as diffusionism."},{"key":"B","text":"In order to study particular cultures as completely as possible, he became skilled in linguistics, the study of languages, and in physical anthropology, the study of human biology and anatomy."},{"key":"C","text":"He argued that human evolution was characterized by a struggle he called the \"survival of the fittest,\" in which weaker races and societies must eventually be replaced by stronger, more advanced races and societies."},{"key":"D","text":"They also focused on important rituals that appeared to preserve a people's social structure, such as initiation ceremonies that formally signify children's entrance into adulthood."},{"key":"E","text":"Thus, in his view, diverse aspects of culture, such as the structure of families, forms of marriage, categories of kinship, ownership of property, forms of government, technology, and systems of food production, all changed as societies evolved."},{"key":"F","text":"Supporters of the theory viewed culture as a collection of integrated parts that work together to keep a society functioning."},{"key":"G","text":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world."}],"answer":"G","explanation":{"answer":"G","type":"段末","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world. 例如,英国人类学家Grafton Elliot Smith和W. J. Perry在信息不充分的基础上错误地认为,农业、制陶和冶金术都起源于古埃及并传播到世界各地。事实上,所有这些文化发展都在世界许多地方的不同时期分别独立发生。\n承接「少数天才民族发明、再扩散」的扩散论概括，补一个具体例子 空前句是 Some attributed virtually every important cultural achievement to the inventions of a few, especially gifted peoples that … then spread to other cultures——这是对扩散论的一般性概括：把重要文化成就归于少数有天赋民族的发明、再扩散开去。第5段到此结束，第6段另起讲 Durkheim。本段末空要补一句为这条概括举出的具体例证。\nFor example 配例 + originated…diffused 复现「单一起源、扩散」，逐条对上 For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry … suggested … that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world 句首 For example 紧承前句概括举例；originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world 正是空前句 the inventions of a few … then spread to other cultures 的具体复现——单一起源（古埃及）、再扩散全球。逻辑连接与词汇复现两类线索全中。","options":{},"choiceEn":"For example, British anthropologists Grafton Elliot Smith and W. J. Perry incorrectly suggested, on the basis of inadequate information, that farming, pottery making, and metallurgy all originated in ancient Egypt and diffused throughout the world. In fact, all of these cultural developments occurred separately at different times in many parts of the world.","clues":["逻辑连接 前句是一般论断，本空宜用 For example 配具体例子 空前句 Some attributed virtually every important cultural achievement to the inventions of a few … then spread to other cultures 是一句概括论断，本空与它构成「概括 → 举例」关系，要求正确句带 For example 一类举例标记，给出落到具体的人和事的例证。","词汇复现 inventions / spread to other cultures 在正确句应以 originated/diffused 复现 空前句的 the inventions of a few 与 then spread to other cultures 是本空核心复现锚点，正确句应再次出现「起源于某地、扩散到别处」的同义说法（originated … diffused throughout the world），用具体例子坐实「单一起源、再扩散」。"]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"There is a marked difference between the education which every one gets from living with others and the deliberate educating of the young. In the former case the education is incidental; it is natural and important, but it is not the express reason of the association. (46) It may be said that the measure of the worth of any social institution is its effect in enlarging and improving experience, but this effect is not a part of its original motive. Religious associations began, for example, in the desire to secure the favor of overruling powers and to ward off evil influences; family life in the desire to gratify appetites and secure family perpetuity; systematic labor, for the most part, because of enslavement to others, etc. (47) Only gradually was the by-product of the institution noted, and only more gradually still was this effect considered as a directive factor in the conduct of the institution. Even today, in our industrial life, apart from certain values of industriousness and thrift, the intellectual and emotional reaction of the forms of human association under which the world's work is carried on receives little attention as compared with physical output."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"But in dealing with the young, the fact of association itself as an immediate human fact, gains in importance. (48) While it is easy to ignore in our contact with them the effect of our acts upon their disposition, it is not so easy as in dealing with adults. The need of training is too evident and the pressure to accomplish a change in their attitude and habits is too urgent to leave these consequences wholly out of account. (49) Since our chief business with them is to enable them to share in a common life we cannot help considering whether or not we are forming the powers which will secure this ability. If humanity has made some headway in realizing that the ultimate value of every institution is its distinctively human effect we may well believe that this lesson has been learned largely through dealings with the young."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"(50) We are thus led to distinguish, within the broad educational process which we have been so far considering, a more formal kind of education – that of direct tuition or schooling. In undeveloped social groups, we find very little formal teaching and training. These groups mainly rely for instilling needed dispositions into the young upon the same sort of association which keeps adults loyal to their group."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"It may be said that the measure of the worth of any social institution is its effect in enlarging and improving experience, but this effect is not a part of its original motive.","refZh":"可以说，衡量任何一种社会机构价值的尺度，在于它对扩充和改善经验所产生的作用，但这种作用并不是它最初动机的一部分。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"It may be said that","lit":"可以说","role":"（形式主语 + 真主语从句引导）","note":"难点： It 是形式主语，that 后才是真主语 It may be said that 里的 It 不指任何东西，是占位。汉语里直接译成「可以说」即可，不要硬译成「它可能被说」这种翻译腔。"},{"en":"the measure of the worth of any social institution is its effect in enlarging and improving experience,","lit":"衡量任何社会机构价值的尺度是它在扩充和改善经验方面的作用","role":"（主语从句的主系表（含两层 of 修饰））","note":"难点： measure 熟词僻义=「尺度/标准」；两层 of 是后置定语 measure 在此不是「测量/措施」，而是「尺度、衡量标准」（熟词僻义 A2）。the measure of the worth of any social institution 是「A of B of C」结构，按汉语习惯要从右往左译：先说 social institution（社会机构）→ worth（价值）→ measure（尺度），即「衡量任何社会机构价值的尺度」。其后 in enlarging and improving experience 是介词短语作 effect 的后置定语，译成「在扩充和改善经验方面的（作用）」。"},{"en":"but this effect is not a part of its original motive.","lit":"但这种作用并不是它最初动机的一部分","role":"（but 引导的并列分句）","note":"难点： this effect 回指 effect in enlarging and improving experience；its 回指 social institution this effect 不能简单译成「这一效果」，要带出它指什么——「扩充和改善经验的这种作用」（或译「这种作用」，因前句刚说过）。its 回指 social institution，译成「它（社会机构）的」。original motive 是「最初的动机/初衷」。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"Only gradually was the by-product of the institution noted, and only more gradually still was this effect considered as a directive factor in the conduct of the institution.","refZh":"人们只是逐渐地才注意到机构的这种副产品，而人们把这种作用视为机构运作中的一个指导性因素，则更加缓慢。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Only gradually was the by-product of the institution noted,","lit":"只是逐渐地，机构的这种副产品才被注意到","role":"（Only 状语前置触发的部分倒装（前一并列分句））","note":"难点： Only + 状语放句首→主谓部分倒装；by-product 回指上句的 effect Only + 副词/介词短语放句首时，主句要部分倒装（A3 长难句信号），was the by-product…noted 还原成正常语序是 the by-product…was noted。by-product（副产品）回指上一句里 effect in enlarging and improving experience——即机构扩充和改善经验这个「附带产生的作用」，不是字面意义的产品。institution 全篇统一译「机构」。"},{"en":"and only more gradually still was this effect considered as a directive factor in the conduct of the institution.","lit":"而更加缓慢地，这种作用才被视为机构运作中的一个指导性因素","role":"（and 连接的并列分句，同为 Only 倒装）","note":"难点： still 与 more gradually 连用，表「更加…」强调程度递进；conduct 熟词僻义=「运作/经营」 more gradually still 中的 still 不是「仍然」，而是修饰 more 的程度副词，意为「更加…」（A7 程度词失察）。this effect 回指 by-product，也就是 46 题锚定的「扩充和改善经验的作用」。directive factor 译「指导性因素」。conduct of the institution 中的 conduct 不是「行为/品行」，而是「运作、经营、管理」（A2 熟词僻义），即「机构的运作」。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"While it is easy to ignore in our contact with them the effect of our acts upon their disposition, it is not so easy as in dealing with adults.","refZh":"尽管在我们与年青人接触时，容易忽视我们的行为对他们性情所产生的影响，但要做到这种忽视，却不像与成年人打交道时那样容易。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"While it is easy to ignore in our contact with them the effect of our acts upon their disposition,","lit":"虽然在我们与他们交往时，容易忽视我们的行为对他们性情的影响","role":"（While 引导的让步状语从句（it 形式主语 + 不定式真主语，宾语后置））","note":"难点： ignore 的宾语被状语 in our contact with them 隔开，要还原；them/their 指年青人 正常语序应为 to ignore the effect of our acts upon their disposition in our contact with them——因为宾语 the effect of our acts upon their disposition 太长，作者把状语 in our contact with them 插到 ignore 和宾语之间（A3 长难句、A4 指代）。读时要把宾语拼回来。them/their 全部指年青人（回扣第二段首句 in dealing with the young）。disposition 译「性情/性格倾向」。while 此处不是「当…时」，而是「虽然/尽管」（让步），与主句的 not so easy 形成对照（A6）。"},{"en":"it is not so easy as in dealing with adults.","lit":"但这并不像与成年人打交道时那样容易","role":"（主句（it 形式主语 + 比较结构 not so…as…））","note":"难点： not so easy as 是比较结构「不如…那样容易」；it 承前指「ignore 这件事」 not so…as… = 不如…那样…（A5 搭配）。主句的 it 与从句的 it 都是形式主语，但承前理解时可以看作指「忽视行为对性情的影响这件事」。比较的两端是「与年青人打交道时（容易忽视）」和「与成年人打交道时（容易忽视）」——意思是「跟年青人在一起时，要忽视很难，比跟成年人在一起时更难做到」。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"Since our chief business with them is to enable them to share in a common life we cannot help considering whether or not we are forming the powers which will secure this ability.","refZh":"由于我们对年青人所做的主要工作，在于使他们能够分享共同的生活，因此我们不能不考虑：自己是否正在培养起一种能保障他们获得这种能力的各种力量。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Since our chief business with them is to enable them to share in a common life","lit":"因为我们与他们打交道的主要任务，是使他们能够分享共同的生活","role":"（Since 引导的原因状语从句）","note":"难点： business 熟词僻义=「事务/职责」；them 指年青人；share in 是固定搭配「分享/参与」 business 在此不是「生意/商业」，而是「事务、要做的事、职责」（A2 熟词僻义）。our chief business with them 译「我们与他们（年青人）打交道时的主要任务/主要事务」。share in 是固定搭配（A5），意为「分享、参与」，share in a common life 译「过共同的生活/分享共同的生活」。Since 在此是「因为」（原因），不是「自从」——判断依据看主句是否陈述结果而非时间起点。"},{"en":"we cannot help considering","lit":"我们禁不住要考虑","role":"（主句主谓）","note":"难点： cannot help doing 固定搭配=「禁不住做…/不得不做…」 cannot help doing 是固定搭配（A5），意为「禁不住做…」「不由得做…」。注意 help 不译「帮助」，doing 是动名词不是名词。译「我们不得不考虑/我们禁不住要考虑」皆可。"},{"en":"whether or not we are forming the powers","lit":"我们是否在培养各种能力","role":"（considering 的宾语从句）","note":"难点： whether or not 引导宾语从句；powers 复数=「能力/力量」 whether or not 译「是否…」。form 在这里不是「形成形状」，而是「培养、形成（能力）」。powers 复数译「各种能力/力量」，不是「权力」。"},{"en":"which will secure this ability.","lit":"（这些能力）将确保这种能力","role":"（which 引导的定语从句，修饰 powers）","note":"难点： this ability 回指 to share in a common life；secure 译「确保/保障」 this ability 不能简单译「这种能力」让读者猜——它回指本句前半的 to share in a common life，即「过共同生活的能力」（A4 代词回指）。translate 时建议把指代显化：「（这种）过共同生活的能力」。secure 在此不是「安全的」（形容词），而是动词「确保、保证、获得」。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"We are thus led to distinguish, within the broad educational process which we have been so far considering, a more formal kind of education – that of direct tuition or schooling.","refZh":"于是，在我们迄今为止一直在讨论的这一广义教育过程之中，我们就有必要区分出一种更为正式的教育——即直接讲授或学校教育。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"We are thus led to distinguish,","lit":"我们因此被引导去区分（出）","role":"（主谓（被动语态作主谓主干））","note":"难点： thus 承上=「因此/由此」；be led to do 译主动「使我们/我们因此」 thus 是承接副词，回指第二段「针对年青人时人们才意识到机构的人性效果」这一论证，译「因此/于是/由此」。be led to do 直译「被引导去做」生硬，转成主动或无主句：「我们于是要去区分」「这就使我们要区分」（A3 + 被动汉化）。distinguish 后的宾语被一个介词短语插入隔开（见下一块），要意识到主干是 distinguish…a more formal kind of education。"},{"en":"within the broad educational process which we have been so far considering,","lit":"在我们迄今为止一直在讨论的广义教育过程之中","role":"（插入语：介词短语作 distinguish 的范围状语 + which 定语从句修饰 process）","note":"难点： 插入语隔开主干宾语；which 定语从句修饰 educational process，have been considering 现在完成进行时 整块是插入语，两端有逗号包围（A3）。within…process 是 distinguish 的范围状语，译「在…之中（区分出）」。which we have been so far considering 是 which 定语从句修饰 process，have been considering 是现在完成进行时强调「一直在…直到现在」，译「我们迄今/到目前为止一直在讨论的」。broad 译「广义的/宽泛的」，与下文 more formal 形成对比。"},{"en":"a more formal kind of education","lit":"一种更为正式的教育","role":"（distinguish 的宾语（被插入语推后了））","note":"难点： more formal 与上文 broad 形成对比；这才是 distinguish 真正的宾语 回到主干：distinguish a more formal kind of education——这才是 distinguish 的宾语，前面那段是插入的范围状语。more formal 是与「广义教育过程」中的「附带式教育」相对的「更正式的（教育）」，译「一种更为正式的教育（形式）」。"},{"en":"– that of direct tuition or schooling.","lit":"——即直接讲授或学校教育（的那种）","role":"（破折号引导的同位语，解释 a more formal kind of education）","note":"难点： 破折号 = 解释说明；that 指代前面的 kind of education；tuition 熟词僻义=「讲授/教学」 破折号在英语里常引出解释/同位语（A5），汉译用「即/也就是」或保留破折号。that 是指示代词，回指 a more formal kind of education，that of direct tuition or schooling 即「直接讲授或学校教育的那种（教育）」。tuition 在此不是「学费」（中国学生最熟的义项），而是「讲授、教学」（A2 熟词僻义，重灾区）。schooling 译「学校教育」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: Restrictions on the use of plastic bags have not been so successful in some regions. “White Pollution” is still going on. Write a letter to the editor(s) of your local newspaper to 1)give your opinions briefly, and 2)make two or three suggestions. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: Restrictions on the use of plastic bags have not been so successful in some regions. “White Pollution” is still going on. Write a letter to the editor(s) of your local newspaper to 1)give your opinions briefly, and 2)make two or three suggestions. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear Editor, I am writing to express my concern about the restrictions on plastic bags, which have not worked as well as we hoped. In my opinion, \"White Pollution\" is still spreading in many places, and it is high time we took real action. To deal with this problem, I would like to make the following suggestions. First, the government should enforce stricter laws and raise the price of plastic bags in supermarkets. Second, citizens ought to be encouraged to carry cloth bags when shopping. Besides, the media could run campaigns to raise public awareness. I hope my ideas will be helpful. Yours sincerely, Li Ming","translation":"尊敬的编辑： 我写这封信是想表达我对塑料袋限制措施的担忧，它们并没有像我们期望的那样奏效。在我看来，\"白色污染\"仍在许多地方蔓延，我们该采取实际行动了。 为解决这一问题，我想提出以下建议。第一，政府应加强立法执法，并提高超市里塑料袋的价格。第二，应鼓励市民购物时自带布袋。此外，媒体可以开展宣传活动以提高公众意识。 希望我的建议能有所帮助。 此致 李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"称呼＋两句表态落实第一段功能","text":"【第 1 段】 称呼＋两句表态落实第一段功能 。开头 Dear Editor 加 I am writing to express my concern... 点明缘由，In my opinion, \"White Pollution\" is still spreading... 简短表态，兑现 give your opinions briefly，没有展开长篇背景。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"First/Second/Besides 三条建议分点清晰","text":"【第 2 段】 First/Second/Besides 三条建议分点清晰 。用 First, the government should... Second, citizens ought to... Besides, the media could... 三条各自成句、主体不同，兑现 make two or three suggestions。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"客气收尾并按要求落款","text":"【第 3 段】 客气收尾并按要求落款 。I hope my ideas will be helpful 收束，落款 Yours sincerely, Li Ming，遵守 Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter，未写真名与地址。"}],"wordCount":106}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1)describe the drawing briefly, 2)explain its intended meaning, and then 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay, you should 1)describe the drawing briefly, 2)explain its intended meaning, and then 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2009-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白漫画，标题是“网络的‘近’与‘远’”","width":"525","height":"566","local":"assets/writing/2009-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a huge web-like space is divided into countless grids. In each grid sits a cubicle, and inside every cubicle a person is bending over a computer, absorbed in work. Above the picture is a thought-provoking title: 'The Nearness and Distance of the Internet.' Simple as the drawing is, it conveys a profound meaning about our digital age. The spider web symbolizes the Internet, which brings distant people close: with a single click we chat with friends thousands of miles away. Yet the isolated grids reveal the other side — while getting 'near' to the far, we are drifting 'far' from those physically around us, trapped in our own screens and indifferent to real neighbours. In my view, such a phenomenon deserves our alertness. The Internet is merely a tool; whether it shortens or widens distances depends on how we use it. For instance, a family sharing one dinner table yet each staring at a phone gains nothing but coldness. Therefore, we should embrace online convenience while cherishing face-to-face communication, so that technology truly serves human bonds rather than replacing them.","translation":"正如漫画生动描绘的那样，一个巨大的蛛网状空间被分割成无数网格。每个网格里都坐着一个格子间，而每个格子间里，都有一个人俯身在电脑前，忙碌不停。画面上方是一个发人深省的标题：“网络的‘近’与‘远’”。\n漫画虽简单，却传达出关于数字时代的深刻寓意。蛛网象征着互联网，它把相隔遥远的人拉近：轻点一下鼠标，我们就能和千里之外的朋友聊天。然而，一个个孤立的格子却揭示了另一面——在与远方变“近”的同时，我们正与近旁的人渐行渐“远”，困在各自的屏幕里，对身边真实的邻里漠然置之。\n在我看来，这种现象值得我们警惕。互联网不过是一件工具；它究竟是缩短还是拉大距离，取决于我们如何使用。比如，一家人围坐同一张餐桌，却各自盯着手机，收获的只有冷漠。因此，我们应当在享受网络便利的同时珍惜面对面的交流，让科技真正服务于人与人的情感联结，而非取而代之。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"描述段落实先描述后点题","text":"【第 1 段】 描述段落实先描述后点题 。本段用『先客观描述再点标题』的走法：开头 As is vividly depicted in the cartoon 一句总起，随后按『空间—格子—人在做什么』层层白描，末句用 a thought-provoking title 把标题引出、埋下钩子，完成 describe the drawing briefly 且不越界抒情。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"寓意段落实细节映射","text":"【第 2 段】 寓意段落实细节映射 。本段用『细节映射社会』：Simple as the drawing is 一句过渡到寓意，再用 The spider web symbolizes... 把蛛网映射为互联网的连接，用 Yet... reveals the other side 的转折托出格子间的疏离，紧扣标题一近一远，达成 explain its intended meaning。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"评论段落实观点加例证","text":"【第 3 段】 评论段落实观点加例证 。本段用『观点加例证收束』：In my view 亮出工具论态度，For instance 一家人同桌各看手机的例子佐证，Therefore 收束给出建议，有判断有例子，兑现 give your comments 而非复述寓意。"}],"wordCount":186}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 B Consider · 2 A tended · 3 D dimmer · 4 B advantage · 5 C turns out · 6 A off · 7 D gradual · 8 C stop · 9 B limited · 10 D backward · 11 D costs · 12 B on · 13 C perform · 14 D for instance · 15 A if · 16 C determine · 17 B for · 18 A Above all · 19 A fundamental · 20 C So far \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 D · 23 A · 24 D · 25 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 A · 27 C · 28 D · 29 A · 30 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 D · 32 B · 33 B · 34 A · 35 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 B · 37 B · 38 D · 39 A · 40 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"选句填空（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 C · 42 E · 43 A · 44 B · 45 G \n（逐题解析见 选句填空（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
